WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/components/feedback/CookieConsentBanner.tsx — a non-blocking bottom-of-viewport GDPR / cookie
  consent banner mounted in <Layout>. Data:
    • useVersionInfo() (from @/api/hooks/useSettings) → /system/version → require_cookie_consent?: boolean
    • lib/cookieConsent → tri-state ConsentState 'unknown'|'accepted'|'declined'
                          ('unknown' = absence of the stored key)
    • useEffect side-effect → setVitalsConsentRequirement / setErrorReporterConsentRequirement(requireConsent)
  Render guard (the ONLY visibility logic): if (!requireConsent) return null; if (consent !== 'unknown') return null
  Composition: shield IconBox + title + body + underlined "Manage preferences"/"Hide details" toggle
               (aria-expanded) + (expanded) two informed-consent <li> cards — "Strictly necessary" with an
               "Always on" badge, and "Performance & error reporting" — + Accept all (primary) / Decline
               non-essential (ghost). NO dismiss button (dismiss != consent; it reappears next visit).
  i18n keys extracted: consent.banner.{title,body,manage,hideDetails,accept,decline},
                       consent.category.essential.{title,body}, consent.category.alwaysOn,
                       consent.category.analytics.{title,body}.

